From: InterGenOS <noreply@intergenos.example>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026
Subject: [PATCH] headermenu: label the zoom-reset control "Reset _Zoom" not "100%"

The hamburger-menu zoom section renders a static "100%" literal as the
reset-to-normal control (action win.zoom-normal). It carries no binding to
the current zoom level (all three zoom actions are stateless), so it never
reflects the actual scale — it is a reset button wearing a value it does not
report. A control that misdescribes its own function violates the principle
that the user must be able to trust what the UI tells them.

This is GNOME/gnome-terminal issue #140 (open since 2019); upstream master
resolves it as a wording fix. Relabel to the translatable "Reset _Zoom" so
the control states what it does. Label only — the win.zoom-normal action,
the GAction state, and font-scale handling are unchanged.

--- a/src/terminal-headermenu.ui
+++ b/src/terminal-headermenu.ui
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
         <attribute name="action">win.zoom-out</attribute>
       </item>
       <item>
-        <attribute name="label">100%</attribute>
+        <attribute name="label" translatable="yes">Reset _Zoom</attribute>
         <attribute name="action">win.zoom-normal</attribute>
       </item>
       <item>
